{"p":"/chat/quick-words","t":"Quick Words","d":"Add custom Quick Words to your experience using Roblox's built-in preset system for safe, cross-age gameplay coordination.","h":"<p><strong>Quick Words</strong> is Roblox's built-in <a href=\"#/docs/chat/preset-system-guidelines\">preset system</a>. Use it to add more Quick Words that follow Roblox's content policies, so players of all ages can safely coordinate gameplay without building a custom preset system.</p>\n<p>Quick Words must focus on gameplay coordination, not social chat, and must not be open-ended questions.</p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"data:image/webp;base64,\" alt=\"The Quick Words page in Creator Hub, showing a draft Coordination category with approved phrases.\" /></p>\n<h2>Configure Quick Words</h2>\n<p>To get started, go to <a href=\"https://create.roblox.com/dashboard/creations\">Creator Hub</a>, select your game, then go to <strong>Configure</strong> &gt; <strong>Chat</strong> &gt; <strong>Quick Words</strong>.</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Add up to three custom categories, with three to ten Quick Words in each category. Each Quick Word must be fewer than 25 characters. Quick Words can only be entered in English, and Roblox automatically translates them into each user's chosen chat language. Custom categories replace the default Roblox categories, while the <strong>General</strong> category remains available to users across games.</li>\n<li>When you publish, Roblox reviews your categories and Quick Words against the safety rules in the <a href=\"#/docs/chat/preset-system-guidelines\">preset system guidelines</a> before they go live. If a phrase isn't approved, revise it and publish again. Review <a href=\"#/docs/chat/preset-system-guidelines\">What is allowed</a> and <a href=\"#/docs/chat/preset-system-guidelines\">What is not allowed</a> for guidance on which phrases pass the policy check.</li>\n<li>Once approved, your Quick Words are automatically available to users in the <strong>Here</strong> and <strong>Global</strong> tabs of the chat window. If you need more time, save your changes as a draft before publishing. You can also revert to the Roblox default Quick Words at any time.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2>Quick Words states</h2>\n<p>Your Quick Words move through four states:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Draft</strong>: You've updated a Quick Word field.</li>\n<li><strong>Pending</strong>: Roblox is checking your Quick Words against the policy.</li>\n<li><strong>Not approved</strong>: Your Quick Words didn't pass the policy check. Revise them and publish again.</li>\n<li><strong>Published</strong>: Your Quick Words passed the policy check and are live in your game.</li>\n</ul>","kid":{"simple":"Quick Words is Roblox's built-in set of ready-made chat phrases that players of all ages can send safely. You can add your own Quick Words for your game, like \"Defend the flag\" or \"Ready\", from the Creator Hub. Roblox checks them against its safety rules before they go live. It is the easy way to help players team up without building your own preset system.","analogy":"Quick Words are like the quick-reply buttons on a phone that say \"On my way\" or \"OK\": tap once and the message is sent, no typing needed.","keyPoints":["Go to Creator Hub, pick your game, then Configure, Chat, Quick Words.","Add up to 3 custom categories, each with 3 to 10 Quick Words.","Each Quick Word must be under 25 characters and written in English. Roblox translates them into each player's chat language automatically.","Custom categories replace Roblox's default categories, but the General category stays available everywhere.","When you publish, Roblox reviews your Quick Words against the preset system guidelines. If one is not approved, fix it and publish again.","Approved Quick Words show up in the Here and Global tabs of the chat window.","You can save a draft before publishing, and you can revert to Roblox's default Quick Words anytime.","Quick Words move through four states: Draft, Pending, Not approved, and Published."],"terms":{"Quick Words":"Roblox's built-in set of safe, ready-made phrases players can send.","preset system":"Any feature that lets players send pre-written messages instead of typing.","category":"A group of related Quick Words, like a Coordination group with \"Follow me\" and \"Wait\".","Creator Hub":"Roblox's website for managing your games, at create.roblox.com.","draft":"Saved changes that are not live yet.","pending":"Roblox is still checking your Quick Words.","policy check":"Roblox's review that makes sure your phrases follow its safety rules.","character":"One letter, number, space, or symbol. \"Need help\" is 9 characters."},"watchOut":["Writing open-ended questions or social phrases like \"How are you\". They will not be approved; stick to gameplay.","Phrases that are 25 characters or longer. Keep them short.","Writing Quick Words in a language other than English. Enter them in English and let Roblox translate.","Forgetting that custom categories replace Roblox's default ones. Make sure your set covers what players need.","Expecting changes right away. They must pass review (Pending) before they are Published."]}}